CONTENT CONFLICT RULE

When two sources conflict:

- LinkedIn is the primary source for current professional headline, experience, education, dates, skills, and certifications.
- GitHub is the primary source for code, repositories, technical stack, installation instructions, and project features.
- The resume can supplement missing information but must not override newer LinkedIn information.
- Owner-provided corrections override all other sources.

Never silently resolve a conflict.

Record conflicts inside:

/content/source-conflicts.json

Do not publish conflicted information until it is confirmed.

